Checks:                 0 / 0, -, Listed 10
Transferred:            5 / 5, 100%
Elapsed time:         0.0s


$ rclone --config data/empty-rclone.conf check prova:config-free provb:replica
2026/11/02 10:18:27 NOTICE: S3 bucket replica: 0 differences found
2026/11/02 10:18:27 NOTICE: S3 bucket replica: 5 matching files
# styles are interchangeable: a connection string with endpoint B keys reads what the named remote provb: wrote

$ rclone --config data/empty-rclone.conf lsf ":s3,provider=Other,endpoint='$S3_B_ENDPOINT',access_key_id=$S3_B_ACCESS_KEY,secret_access_key=$S3_B_SECRET_KEY:replica"
via-connection-string/
via-env/

==================== F. Credentials really are checked ====================
# endpoint B's keys against endpoint A must fail

$ rclone --config data/empty-rclone.conf lsd :s3: --s3-provider Other --s3-endpoint "$S3_A_ENDPOINT" --s3-access-key-id "$S3_B_ACCESS_KEY" --s3-secret-access-key "$S3_B_SECRET_KEY" --retries 1 --low-level-retries 1
2026/11/02 10:18:27 ERROR : error listing: operation error S3: ListBuckets, https response error StatusCode: 403, RequestID: , HostID: , api error InvalidAccessKeyId: The Access Key Id you provided does not exist in our records.
2026/11/02 10:18:27 NOTICE: Failed to lsd with 2 errors: last error was: operation error S3: ListBuckets, https response error StatusCode: 403, RequestID: , HostID: , api error InvalidAccessKeyId: The Access Key Id you provided does not exist in our records.
(exit code 1)

